inar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IgorMinar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IgorMinar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IgorMinar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IgorMinar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IgorMinar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IgorMinar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":681,"closed_issues":22796,"state":"open","created_at":"2018-01-18T16:52:20Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T09:12:24Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":5,"created_at":"2016-06-10T18:48:13Z","updated_at":"2022-04-28T16:08:15Z","closed_at":"2022-03-28T16:38:36Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"- **I'm submitting a ...**\n- [x] bug report\n- [ ] feature request\n- [ ] support request => Please do not submit support request here, see note at the top of this template.\n\n**Current behavior**\n\nSetting options like this:\n\n```\n        this.headers = new Headers({ 'accept': \"application/json;odata=verbose\" });\n        this.options = new RequestOptions({ headers: this.headers });\n```\n\nIt works if I use http:\n\n```\nreturn this._http.get(url, this.options)\n  .map((res: Response) => res.json());\n```\n\nI look at the headers in Fiddler I see:\n`accept: application/json;odata=verbose`\n\nIf I try the same thing with JsonP:\n\n```\nreturn this._jsonp.get(url, this.options)\n  .map((res: Response) => res.json()); \n```\n\nThen in the Fiddler I see this header:\n`Accept: */*`\n\n**Expected/desired behavior**\n\nHeaders from options passed to JsonP.get() are not used.\n- **What is the motivation / use case for changing the behavior?**\n\nI am trying to access a SharePoint oData source.  The bad news is that http.get() gets a CORS violation error.  The good news is that jsonp.get() gets a document, but it's XML.  \n\nI am trying to pass accept headers with JsonP and they are not getting set.\n- **Please tell us about your environment:**\n  Windows 10, VS Code, Chrome \n  Remote SharePoint site\n- **Angular version:** 2.0.0-beta.X \n- **Browser:**\n  Chrome\n- **Language:** \n  Typscript\n","closed_by":{"login":"dylhunn","id":7135246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMzUyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7135246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn","html_url":"https://github.com/dylhunn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylhunn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/9141/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/9141/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}